# Expectation record for 02_constant_expressions/008_float_constant_folding.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 008_float_constant_folding
area               = 02_constant_expressions
description        = Floating constant folding over exactly representable dyadic rationals at fixed print precision -- arithmetic, grouping, comparison, truncation and int/float conversion -- each computation instantiated once folded and once over volatile operands
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined behaviour and depends on no unspecified behaviour, which is the
precondition both differential oracles rest on rather than a stylistic preference: undefined
behaviour would license either compiler to do anything at all, so a divergence between them would
prove nothing about either. The paragraphs below are the written argument required of every program
in this suite; the warning gate and the sanitizer gate are its machine half.
EVERY FLOATING VALUE IN THE PROGRAM IS A DYADIC RATIONAL exactly representable in binary floating
point. Enumerated from the source rather than characterised loosely, the operands are 0.125, 0.25,
0.5, 0.75, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.25, 3.0, 3.75, 4.0, 7.0 and 8.0, together with -3.75, six of them
appearing in single precision as well as in double; and every result is one too: the sums,
differences, products and quotients are 0.75, 2.25, 3.0, 0.125, 3.5, 0.875, 1.75, 2.5, 5.5, 7.0 and
-0.75. Note that 3.5 occurs only as a result and never as an operand, and that nothing outside those
two lists is written or computed anywhere in the file. No result needs rounding in either binary32 or
binary64, which is what makes the equality comparisons here exact questions rather than tolerance
questions, and what lets a float result be widened to double and compared with the double result of
the same expression.
NO DIVISOR IS ZERO. The program divides in twelve places -- six folded expressions and their six
runtime twins -- and every divisor there is one of 8.0, 2.0, 4.0 and 4.0f, each written as a literal
or held in a volatile object initialized from one and never modified afterwards, so no divisor can
become zero at run time either.
NO OPERATION OVERFLOWS TO INFINITY AND NONE PRODUCES A NaN. The largest magnitude anywhere is 8.0
against a minimum representable range of at least 1e37 and the smallest is 0.125, so there is no
overflow, no underflow and no invalid operation, and every result is exact. Neither an infinity nor a
NaN is produced, compared or printed anywhere in the program, so no unordered comparison arises and
no identity assumption about either is made or needed.
EVERY FLOATING-TO-INTEGER CONVERSION IS WELL INSIDE int's RANGE BY CONSTRUCTION, which forecloses the
one undefined case specific to this program: C11 makes the conversion undefined when the truncated
value cannot be represented in the destination. The truncations are (int)3.75 and (int)-3.75, giving
3 and -3, and the round-trip is (int)((double)7 / 2.0 * 2.0), giving exactly 7 because every
intermediate is exactly representable; each conversion is written with an explicit (int) cast so it
is stated in the source rather than inferred. The int-to-floating conversions of 5, 7 and 9 are exact
in both precisions.
NO SIGNED INTEGER OVERFLOW IS POSSIBLE: the only integer values in the program are the small
conversion inputs 5, 7 and 9, the truncation results 3, -3 and 7, the 0/1 results of the comparisons,
and the 0 the program returns. No integer is ever added, multiplied or negated, and no shift, no
remainder and no integer division appears at all.
NO FLOATING VALUE IS TYPE-PUNNED. Nothing is reinterpreted through a pointer or a union, so nothing
depends on representation, on byte order or on padding, and no aliasing rule can be broken. There is
no pointer arithmetic and no array subscript anywhere in the file, no address is taken, and nothing
depends on the relative addresses of unrelated objects.
EVERY VOLATILE OBJECT IS INITIALIZED AT ITS DECLARATION, every folded local is initialized from a
constant expression and every runtime local is initialized from volatile reads before it is used, so
no storage is read uninitialized. No object is modified anywhere after its initialization, so nothing
is modified twice between two sequence points.
EVERY MACRO PARAMETER APPEARS EXACTLY ONCE IN ITS BODY, and the macros expand to fully parenthesized
expressions, so no operand is evaluated twice and no volatile object is read twice within a single
expression. Where a computation needs the same value in two places, two DISTINCT volatile objects
supply it rather than one object read twice. Every result is stored in its own named variable and
only those variables are passed to printf, so no call receives a side-effecting argument and no
argument-evaluation order is ever observable.
EVERY VALUE PASSED TO printf FOR A FLOATING CONVERSION IS A double: the float results are widened by
an explicit (double) cast, which states in the source the default argument promotion a variadic call
would apply anyway.
NO HEADER IS NAMED ANYWHERE and the single libc prototype the program needs, printf, is declared by
hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`. bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a
bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard I/O header (docs/project-guide.md, "9 bundled freestanding
headers"), so a directive naming that header would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a) while
succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by the
compiler under test. Nothing in the file is a GCC extension, so no include exception and no gate
deviation is available to area 02 and none is needed; the corpus has exactly two header exceptions,
area 07's stdarg.h and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12. Nor could a floating-point
program reach for its usual headers here: math.h, fenv.h and complex.h are in neither bundled set, so
no math-library function is called or declared, no floating-point environment is inspected and no
complex type is used -- the program links against libc alone under -static, which is the one linkage
mode both compilers spell identically. float.h IS bundled and is deliberately left unnamed all the
same: every constant this program needs is written out literally, which is what keeps it reproducible
from one source file and its record alone.
THIS RECORD DECLARES NO WARNING-GATE DEVIATION: no ub_audit_flags key appears above, so the program
is audited under the suite's full default gate, which is what area 02 requires of every one of its
eight programs. MEASURED: the program compiles with no diagnostic whatsoever under -Wall -Wextra
-pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror in sixteen invocations -- each of the four
reference drivers, once in the harness's own compile-only form and again at -O0, -O1 and -O2 -- which
is what the explicit (double) and (int) casts are for. It also builds and runs clean under the
sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all, dynamically linked and native:
the instrumented binary ran to completion with exit status 0, wrote nothing to standard error,
produced none of the sanitizer runtimes' diagnostic markers, and printed the golden stream below byte
for byte. That gate is load-bearing for this program in particular rather than ceremonial, because
UBSan's float-cast-overflow check is exactly what would catch a floating-to-integer conversion whose
truncated value did not fit the destination -- the one undefined case a floating-point program of
this shape could plausibly contain. Both gates are reference-compiler-only and are never applied to
bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing. All four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled, and no expected-divergence marker is attached. These notes exist to
record how that was achieved, because a program in this area could easily have had to narrow:
constant evaluation reaches straight into the type system, which is where the four supported
targets differ, and floating-point determinism rests on three deliberate choices, each verified
by measurement rather than assumed.
THE AREA RULE THAT ORGANISES THE WHOLE FILE: print at fixed precision with margin, and make no
NaN or infinity identity assumption. FIRST, THE VALUES. Every floating value in this program,
operand and result alike, is a DYADIC RATIONAL -- a finite sum of powers of two -- so each is
exactly representable in binary32 and binary64 alike and every operation is exact, and no
target's rounding mode, evaluation order or excess-precision behaviour can change a printed
digit. A value such as 0.1 would be inexact, and its printed digits could then legitimately
differ between an x87 double-extended intermediate and an IEEE binary64 one. SECOND, THE
PRECISION. Every value is printed with an explicit precision, %.6f or %.9f for the two division
results, short enough that no rounding decision is ever at stake: that is fixed precision with
margin rather than a shortest-round-trip rendering, and the margin matters because a rendering
that printed as many digits as it needed would expose an intermediate that happened to carry
extra precision. THIRD, THE TYPES. Only float and double are used -- IEEE binary32 and binary64
on all four supported targets -- and the widest floating type is deliberately absent.
THE TWO TYPES IN USE HAVE THE SAME WIDTH AND THE SAME BYTE ORDER ON ALL FOUR TARGETS, WHICH IS
THE CONCRETE REASON NO TARGET IS DROPPED AND NO ORACLE IS DISABLED HERE. sizeof(float) was
MEASURED at 4 bytes and sizeof(double) at 8 bytes on x86-64, i686, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 alike,
and every one of the four is little-endian (docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines
457-462, which records the byte order of every supported target; that table does not state
floating-point widths, so those are cited to measurement rather than to it). A float result and a
double result therefore denote the same value on every backend, which is what turns oracle (b)
here into a question about code generation rather than a question about representation -- the
exact opposite of the widest floating type, whose representation does differ across these targets
and which is excluded for that reason in its own paragraph further below.
COMPARING FLOATING VALUES WITH == IS LEGITIMATE HERE, AND THE REASON IS EXACT REPRESENTABILITY
RATHER THAN THE GATE'S SILENCE. -Wfloat-equal is deliberately not a member of the suite's default
warning gate, so the compiler says nothing about the equality comparisons in this program; that
silence is permission, not justification. The justification is that both sides of every
comparison are dyadic rationals exactly representable in the format the comparison is performed
in, so (0.5 + 0.25) == 0.75 asks a question with a determinate answer on every target, and a
float result widened to double compares equal to the double result of the same expression because
both are the same exact value rather than two values that happen to be close. MEASURED, so the
distinction is not theoretical: adding -Wfloat-equal to the gate raises 21 diagnostics on this
program, every one of them on a comparison that is nonetheless exact. A program comparing inexact
values would owe a tolerance instead, and would belong in area 13 rather than here.
FLT_EVAL_METHOD IS THE IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED PROPERTY THIS PROGRAM HAD TO DEFEAT, AND IT IS
DEFEATED BY CONSTRUCTION RATHER THAN BY A RESTRICTION. i686 evaluates floating expressions in
x87 extended precision -- FLT_EVAL_METHOD 2 -- while x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 do not, so a
program that printed a value whose last digits depended on intermediate precision would diverge
on i686 through no fault of the compiler, and would have to narrow its target list or carry an
expected-divergence marker. Excess precision cannot perturb a value that is already exact in
every format involved, which is exactly what choosing dyadic rationals guarantees. So all twelve
cells stay byte-comparable, no target is dropped, no oracle is disabled and this record carries
no marker. The alternative -- restricting to the three targets with FLT_EVAL_METHOD 0 -- would
have removed the only ILP32 backend and the only x87 evaluation model from the comparison, which
is where a floating-point code-generation defect is most likely to hide.
long double IS NEVER USED, NEVER COMPUTED WITH AND NEVER PRINTED. Its representation was MEASURED
at 16, 12, 16 and 16 bytes across x86-64, i686, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- x87 80-bit against IEEE
binary128 -- so it is the one floating type whose value-level cross-backend comparison is not
sound, and a printed value of that type could not be compared across backends at all. That
comparison is owned by 13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted.c, which carries a
RECORDED EXCLUSION for it -- oracle_b disabled, with the measured representations as its recorded
reason -- together with the marker XD-TYPE-LONGDOUBLE-001, class comparison_excluded, scope oracle_b,
which the format REQUIRES beside such a narrowing: a disabled oracle is reported XFAIL,
which claims the authority of a documented limitation, so the marker is what carries that claim
while the recorded reason explains it. That class is the one value naming no observation, and it is
the value that arm requires, because no cross-backend value comparison is attempted for that program
-- the record switches the arm off, so a class describing a comparison result would assert a
disagreement nothing measured. It excuses the cross-backend arm alone, and a same-target
disagreement there is still a FINDING -- so nothing is lost by keeping the type out of a program
whose subject is the constant folder. No
feature is dropped here for being awkward: the type is tested where its awkwardness can be
accounted for, and this paragraph is the explicit statement of why it is absent from this
program. Also deliberately elsewhere, so this program does not duplicate them: general float
and int conversion boundaries (13_floating_point/002),
finite ordering breadth (13_floating_point/003), sizeof and _Alignof facts (004_sizeof_alignof.c
in this area), and the f suffix's typing effect observed through _Generic
(005_integer_constant_suffixes.c in this area) -- here the f suffix appears only as part of a
computed value. NaN and infinity behaviour is owned by nobody: the area rule forecloses it
deliberately, so neither is ever produced.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) were MEASURED at 4 bytes on i686 and 8
bytes on x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 (docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines
457-462), so no plain long, no size_t, no ptrdiff_t, no sizeof result and no pointer value is
printed anywhere. The format vocabulary is deliberately minimal and is exactly %d for integers
and %.6f and %.9f for floating values; nothing width-dependent or representation-dependent
reaches a format string, and no address is printed.
PLAIN-char SIGNEDNESS. Plain char was MEASURED as signed on x86-64 and i686 and unsigned on
AArch64 and RISC-V 64. No plain-char value is printed and no printed line depends on that
choice.
EVERY DEFAULT ARGUMENT PROMOTION AND EVERY NARROWING IS WRITTEN OUT RATHER THAN IMPLIED. Each
float passed to the variadic printf carries an explicit (double) cast, so the promotion the
standard performs is stated in the source, and each floating-to-integer conversion carries an
explicit (int) cast. That is what keeps the program clean under the default gate's -Wconversion
and -Wsign-conversion, for which area 02 sanctions no deviation, and it means a reader can see
every type change without inferring one.
THE TWO-VARIANT PAIRING IS THE ASSERTION. Every fold_ line is printed with the runtime line that
recomputes the same value from volatile operands, and their agreement is what the program exists
to check: without the runtime twin, optimization would substitute the folder's answer for the
backend's and a floating-point code-generation defect would escape detection entirely. The
all_pairs_agree line is the program's own cross-check that all 26 folded values equal their
runtime twins, and it is redundant to the individual lines above it rather than a substitute for
them.
WHAT WOULD LEGITIMATELY BREAK THAT, AND HOW IT MUST THEN BE HANDLED. A conforming target whose
float or double were not IEEE binary32 and binary64, or which evaluated double expressions in a
wider format in a way that survived to the printed digits, could print different lines without
being defective. That would be an implementation-defined divergence rather than a compiler
defect, and it must then be recorded as an expected divergence with this record's target list
narrowed and the reason stated in this field -- never left to surface as a finding against a
backend that did nothing wrong, and never resolved by dropping the floating coverage this program
exists to provide.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET: NOT ENGAGED, VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSERTED. C11 5.2.1 leaves the
members of the execution character set and their codes implementation-defined, so a program
that printed a character's numeric code, or rendered a literal as bytes, would owe an
accounting here. This one owes none: it contains no character constant at all -- checked
mechanically, by stripping comments and string literals and finding zero -- and derives no
printed VALUE from a character. It declares no _Static_assert either, so its only string
literals are its 55 printf format strings, and those contribute nothing but fixed label text
that is byte-identical in all twelve cells of the matrix and in the golden record below. There
is therefore no code to pin and nothing to narrow. That is precisely what distinguishes this
program from 004_sizeof_alignof.c and 007_string_literal_constants.c in the same area, both of
which do print character codes and both of which pin every code they print with a
_Static_assert for that reason.
HERMETIC AND DETERMINISTIC. Every input is a literal in the source: nothing is read from the
clock, the environment, the command line, a file or a socket, and nothing is written anywhere.
Output is one line per semantic property claimed, in a fixed order, so a single divergent line
names the construct that produced it. No address or pointer value is printed, there is no
randomness, no locale-dependent formatting and no data-dependent iteration order, and the
program returns 0 -- well inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is
truncated by the operating system.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the gnu17 reference driver for each of the four
targets at -O0, -O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and executed natively on x86-64 and
under the target's QEMU user-mode runner for i686, AArch64 and RISC-V 64. Every one of the
twelve produced the same 1,085 bytes over 55 lines and exited with status 0, and the golden
block below was transcribed from that capture rather than typed. That is why cross-backend
comparison is sound for this program, why oracle (b) is enabled with no narrowing, and why
oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. Those figures are exact and dated to this
branch, so re-measure rather than trust them; and if a printed value ever changes, it is a
finding to be reported with its minimized reproducer and its exact reproduction commands, never
an expectation to be regenerated into agreement. A floating-point golden record is the easiest
kind to talk oneself into refreshing, which is why that direction is written down here beside
it.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
